x)=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        DNE\n\nCurrent part:\n\nWhat is the average rate of change of the function $f(x)$ over the interval $x\\in [\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}+h],$ where $h>0$ is a parameter? Express your answer in terms of $h.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $\\frac{Δf}{Δx}\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" 13194139533712 true] [17592186247943 1113 #uuid "7fa50f56-e390-5647-861f-69dfd6d9b85e" 13194139533712 true] [17592186247943 1138 false 13194139533712 true] [17592186247943 1145 "We have the function $f(x)=5sin⁡(2x).$ Notice that we are given the length $h$ of the interval. So, the average rate of change of $f$ over this interval is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{Δf}{Δx}=\\frac{f(a+h)-f(a)}{h},\n$$\n\nwith $a=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ Substituting into the formula and simplifying gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{Δf}{Δx} & =\\frac{f(a+h)-f(a)}{h} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(\\frac{\\pi }{2}+h)-f(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}{h} \\\\  & =\\frac{5sin⁡(2(\\frac{\\pi }{2}+h))-5sin⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})}{h} \\\\  & =\\frac{5sin⁡(\\pi +2h)-5sin⁡(\\pi )}{h} \\\\  & =\\frac{5sin⁡(\\pi +2h)-5(0)}{h} \\\\  & =\\frac{5sin⁡(\\pi +2h)}{h} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{h}sin⁡(\\pi +2h).\\e